    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0204" n="184" sameAs="frus:frus1948v01p1/pg184"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.AA/3–2548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Italy </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-03-23T13:00:00-05:00">March 25, 1948—1
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>826. For the Ambassador. As you know, Dept has proposed US, UK and France request
                    Security Council reconsider Ital application UN membership in light GA favorable
                    recommendation. Brit FonOff feels, however, gesture at this time might detract
                    from effectiveness Trieste declaration and could in any event be met by
                    Communist counter propaganda to effect USSR favored admission Italy and Balkans,
                    but Western powers blocking Soviet desires.</p>
                <p>Dept urgently desires your views in light present Ital situation, as well as any
                    informal Ital reaction you may have.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
